WEBVTT

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.066
who function well under intense stress.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:04.741
Now, if you're screening
for Navy SEALS, I totally get it,

00:01:04.765 --> 00:01:07.930
but the capacity to function under duress

00:01:07.954 --> 00:01:12.876
is totally irrelevant
if the actual job is stocking shelves

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.676
or folding T-shirts,
unless of course it's Black Friday.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.636
Clara is a classic example.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:20.476
We met in CY's early days

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.602
while she was waiting
for her job interview.

00:01:22.626 --> 00:01:25.936
Clara was 25 years old,
had cerebral palsy

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.126
and used a walker.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.786
She seemed quite nervous,

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:32.426
but she was likable,
intelligent and talkative.